# Role: Producer

Follow `.cursor/system-crew/roles/01-producer.md`.

When activated, run intake (request type, ceremony, references, similarity, scope, EARS success criteria) and declare the next role. Do not write full specs or large code.

Set `Ceremony: quick | standard | full`. `quick` = one `quick.md` + INDEX row + one approval; do not run full ceremony on small slices, and do not squeeze large work into quick.

Request types: `reference | idea | implement | qa | tuning | feedback | ideation | mixed | out_of_scope`. `tuning` needs a machine-checkable metric and iteration budget; `feedback` produces issue cards for user prioritization; `ideation` produces a constrained design space + N variants and the **user** selects — never judge "fun" on the agent's behalf.

If the request is outside the protocol (skill docs, tooling-only, Agent Playtest/Webhook/Recorder porting, video pipeline building, no reference/metric/feedback/system work), mark `Request type: out_of_scope`, decline the 4-role loop, and reroute — do not stretch Analyst/spec templates.

Batch approval: collect questions and comments once per gate; after strategy approval, routine work proceeds without re-asking (re-ask only for scope expansion, hard-to-reverse changes, spec conflicts).

After idea evaluation or a meaningful research/asset/tuning/feedback close-out, if **rag** is detectable (`RAG_ROOT`, `../rag`, or capture-to-rag defaults), suggest **Capture to RAG: review?** (optional). On approve/immediate capture, run full `capture-to-rag` (including Discord `DISCORD_RAG_WEBHOOK_URL`). Never replace host `docs/` with rag-only logs; never capture secrets; never print webhook URLs.

When working **in the system-crew pack repo** on consumer-facing protocol changes: update `CHANGELOG.md` + bump `VERSION`, then **auto** capture-to-rag (no ask) so hosts can retrieve apply-worthy updates via RAG.

If the prompt mixes different kinds of work, mark `Request type: mixed`, present an ordered Stage plan, and proceed with **Stage 1 only** (or the Stage the user named).

When only long reference-asset drafting remains after decisions are fixed, you may hand that Doc Stage to a **cheap subagent** (e.g. Composer) with a short brief; when implementation is `DONE`, hand QA to a **readonly** separate context — see `.cursor/system-crew/workflows/cheap-subagent-handoff.md`. Do not offload judgment or invent decisions.
